# Proposed canonical effective-speech feedback

Preparation only, after reviewed implementation `5a17a9da11f1c19ef369e6b629bae10aa87b2b6f` and closed evidence `f1f26262d1331f17a27acf6903d849ef3047bdf6`. No code, native instruction, provider/account setting, saved case or paid ledger is changed by this proposal.

## Demonstrated problem

Canonical `applyOperations` already applies ordered operations. `set-text` updates a text item's displayed text and, if speech is present at that point, its speech.text. It does not create speech. A later set-speech may then replace speech independently. The accepted held-out slot0 proposal first set long speech and then set shorter text; the final retained canonical document speaks the shorter text. Its QA referenced details absent from that final speech. We must preserve these semantics and original evidence.

Current operation schema lacks that description. Admin validate-proposal computes the canonical document but returns only valid/project/revision/quality; native proposeEdits discards that result and returns proposed/applied flags. The agent therefore does not receive canonical final speech for a subsequent self-check.

## Proposed descriptions: exact wording

On the shared set-text operation schema:

> Set the displayed text of a text item. If the item has speech when this operation executes, also replace that speech's text with these exact bytes; this does not create speech. Operations execute in array order. A later set-text can overwrite text supplied by an earlier set-speech. To intentionally keep different displayed and spoken text, put set-speech after set-text.

On set-speech:

> Set or remove this item's speech without changing displayed text. Operations execute in array order: a later set-text on a text item with speech also replaces speech.text. Review canonical effective speech after all operations.

On native proposeEdits:

> Propose bounded edits to the admitted revision for the operator to accept. Operations are evaluated in array order. The result reports canonical effective speech after every operation, when it fits the bounded response; use it to check your proposed speech and QA claims. An unavailable speech view is not complete coverage. This tool does not apply changes or approve anything.

These describe existing behavior; no prompt/default block is edited and no speech is silently restored, coerced, normalized or truncated. Description changes alter the shipped tool-schema bytes, so any future paid admission needs a newly reviewed pinned schema digest and guard manifest. Closed schema/adapter evidence remains immutable.

## Proposed success contract

Add a strict neutral `studioProposalValidationResultSchema` in `packages/studio-contracts/src/production.ts`. Preserve existing valid:true/projectId/revision/quality fields and add `effectiveSpeech`. Return it only after current authentication, delegated authority, grant/project/revision, canonical operation, role-coverage, asset and exact source eligibility checks succeed.

`effectiveSpeech` has a versioned common header:

- version:1; projectId; baseRevision; language.
- operationsDigest: Admin studioHash(command.operations), preserving array order and including all operations. Exclude random idempotency key so equivalent ordered edits identify equally.
- scriptDigest: existing Admin scriptHash(projectedDocument), retaining the exact established script identity including ordered IDs, speech, voice/settings and pronunciation references. Do not invent a second approval hash.
- speechItemCount; spokenItemCount; suppressedItemCount; emptyItemCount; exactTextUtf8Bytes across all speech-bearing items. Counts may overlap explicitly: an item can be both suppressed and empty.
- view discriminator: inline or unavailable.

For view:inline, complete:true and items contains **every** speech-bearing item in `orderedStudioSpeech(projectedDocument)` order. Each strict entry contains itemId, trackId, startFrame, durationInFrames, role, suppressed, text and spoken (exactly !suppressed && text.length>0). Text is copied byte-for-byte, including whitespace. Whitespace-only text remains visible as such; this feedback does not override existing narration preflight rejecting blank/too-long speech. No privileged source bytes, internal error details or arbitrary component properties are included.

The metadata/order helps distinguish simultaneous roles and suppressed items without forcing a layout. Provider/model/voice/settings/pronunciation identity remains bound by scriptDigest; this inline view is explicitly a transcript/role view, **not** proof those dependencies were fully reviewed, a narration approval or a paid-provider input certificate.

For view:unavailable, complete:false, reason:INLINE_BYTE_LIMIT, inlineByteLimit:30720 and no items/text field. Preserve the complete header/counts/digests. Canonical validation may still succeed; exceeding feedback size must not invalidate an otherwise valid project or impose a project/layout cap. Do not include a misleading partial prefix. The retained canonical preview remains the operator's authoritative full view. This narrow proposal does not add a pagination endpoint, registry or prompt database; if full model inspection of oversized proposals becomes required, design a separate immutable projection-read contract explicitly.

Measure UTF-8 JSON bytes of the entire effectiveSpeech envelope, including escaping and metadata. Emit inline only if <=30720 bytes and <=1000 items (existing document limit). Otherwise return the small unavailable envelope. Bound check is exact serialized bytes, not character count. It must not increase existing request/result/stream limits. This is a deliberate bounded degradation: oversized projects remain editable, but the model cannot honestly claim complete canonical transcript inspection from this response.

Native proposeEdits parses the successful result, checks projectId/base revision and operationsDigest against its submitted command, then returns `{proposed:true, applied:false, validation:{valid:true,projectId,revision,effectiveSpeech}}` to the next native turn. Do not return the duplicate model-authored quality report in this feedback. The entire native result must fit 32768 serialized UTF-8 bytes; if metadata pushes the complete view over that bound, use the unavailable variant. The 30720-byte inline allowance leaves room for the strictly bounded wrapper, but still measure the actual complete result. For native operationsDigest verification, reuse the existing canonical-hash algorithm in a shared server-only helper, with fixed vectors proving byte equivalence to Admin studioHash; no cross-app import or new approval/cache algorithm. Preserve proposal event contents and existing retained-generation manifest shape; Admin retained read already reconstructs the full canonical document. Existing typed malformed-property and role-coverage error paths stay separate and unchanged. A malformed/mismatched success envelope is a bounded tool failure, never trusted transcript data.

Canonical speech is untrusted editorial data, not an instruction channel. The tool description identifies it as data; neither exact text nor a quality self-rating grants authority. A returned view enables inspection but cannot certify fidelity, depth, scripture-echo or creative quality.

## Meaningful unpaid tests before implementation review

1. Actual slot0 ordered operations: set-speech then set-text yields the final short canonical speech and digest; earlier long prose remains absent. Reversed operation order intentionally yields different speech. Assert display text and speech separately; no semantic change to applyOperations.
2. set-text on an item without speech does not create it; set-speech:null removal, empty and suppressed speech remain explicit. Custom roles, different tracks, simultaneous starts and opposite insertion/timeline order preserve canonical ordering with no required bridge/settle arrangement.
3. scriptDigest equals existing scriptHash; voice/settings/pronunciation edits change the digest as existing identity dictates, while transcript text is untouched. Operation reorder changes operationsDigest. No approval, narration dispatch or project mutation.
4. Multibyte text/JSON escaping exactly below/at/above30720 bytes; up to1000 items. Inline is complete or absent, never clipped. Oversize succeeds with unavailable status and no full-coverage claim. No unbounded property echo.
5. Wrong authority/project/revision, invalid fields, false role coverage and ineligible/wrong-language source still fail before success feedback. Preserve current bounded typed errors and unrelated error redaction.
6. Native local MockLanguageModelV3 first proposes actual operations; next turn observes exact projected speech and can produce a revised proposal. Malformed/mismatched success envelope fails safely. Valid typed-error repair still works; no-progress/replay and deadline bounds remain effective. No provider calls or auto-run quality retries.
7. Affected Admin/neutral/native tests, typechecks/builds and fixed-base Standards/Spec review, hooks. No paid/creative acceptance claim from deterministic correction.

## Boundaries and recommendation

Implement only the shared descriptions and bounded success feedback, reusing canonical projection/order/hash and existing native tool transport. No default prompt tuning, universal style rules, set-text semantic change, account changes, media, registration, apply/approval/publication or paid evaluation. Any future provider test needs fresh exact schema/request limits and separate authorization. Keep feature acceptance in progress.
